{
    "name": "E2E Kafka - SendMessage and NewMessage",
    "description": "Sends a message with a key and headers to the topic topic-2-jirka with SendMessage and checks that NewMessage consumes it back from the same topic with the same value, key and headers.",
    "notes": {
        "5b295c9c-3514-4b0b-b2ba-471f4fa8fa7c": {
            "x": 64,
            "y": 304,
            "width": 672,
            "height": 256,
            "content": "## ⚠️ Test data assumption\n\nThe topic **topic-2-jirka** must exist on the broker of the connected account. The test user can't create topics (TOPIC_AUTHORIZATION_FAILED), so the components never create it.\n\nNewMessage uses the fixed consumer group **appmixer-e2e-kafka** with **From Beginning** on. The group's committed offset is what makes the flow race-free: a message SendMessage produces before the consumer has joined the group is still delivered when it joins. Don't rename the group, and keep the topic free of other traffic: the Assert checks the first message the trigger receives.\n\nThe account should carry a **TLS CA** (the broker's self-signed certificate) next to its SASL credentials. Before 1.2.7 any TLS CA, key or certificate made every connection fail with `fs is not defined`."
        }
    },
